# 1. Product Identity and Vision

**Project:** OrayCSS  
**Category:** Utility-first CSS framework and CSS generation toolchain  
**Primary language:** Modern JavaScript  
**Styling language:** CSS  
**Package name target:** `oraycss`, subject to availability and naming-conflict checks  
**CLI command:** `oraycss`  
**Primary execution environment:** Node.js for compilation; modern browsers for the resulting CSS  
**Dependency policy:** Zero mandatory third-party dependencies; target zero external npm dependencies altogether  
**Primary interface:** HTML classes plus a standalone CLI  
**Compatibility goal:** Usable alongside vanilla HTML, JavaScript, TypeScript, React, Vue, Svelte, Astro, and other tools that output HTML or contain recognizable class attributes.

The central vision is:

> OrayCSS transforms utility-first styling into a precise visual design instrument. It combines the speed of atomic CSS, the expressive power of modern CSS, the consistency of a thoughtful design system, and the elegance of premium digital product design—all without requiring a JavaScript UI framework, browser runtime, external service, or third-party runtime dependency.

OrayCSS should make excellent design easier to achieve without forcing every website into the same aesthetic.

It should support everything from clean SaaS dashboards and editorial websites to immersive portfolios, futuristic interfaces, sophisticated commerce experiences, minimalist applications, and polished product landing pages.

## Four product pillars

### Pillar A — Effortless utility

Developers should write expressive classes directly in markup and compile only the required styles.

### Pillar B — Premium design foundations

Typography, spacing, visual hierarchy, shadows, borders, surfaces, gradients, motion, and design tokens should work together as a cohesive system.

### Pillar C — Standalone performance

The framework should generate ordinary CSS ahead of time. The finished website must not need OrayCSS JavaScript running in the browser.

### Pillar D — Freedom and accessibility

OrayCSS should work with plain HTML, existing CSS, established JavaScript frameworks, custom design systems, keyboard navigation, and reduced-motion preferences.

