};
```

Define how semantic colors, foreground contrast tokens, breakpoints, and default tokens interact. Validate configuration and reject invalid values with clear diagnostics.

A JavaScript configuration file is executable code; load a trusted project configuration through standard module loading, and document that developers should not run unknown configurations without reviewing them.

Consider an optional CSS-first theme syntax in a later phase, but do not implement a fragile partial parser for complex CSS solely to mimic another framework.

## 11.3 Light and dark themes

Ensure theme tokens work in both light and dark contexts.

Provide a sensible default palette and clear customization instructions. Do not assume every website needs a dark theme, and do not force a global dark-mode toggle onto the consuming application.

Preserve user choice, existing page styles, and system-preference behavior according to configuration.

