# 13. Preflight and Existing CSS Compatibility

If OrayCSS provides a baseline reset, it must be optional or clearly documented and carefully scoped to its purpose.

A developer should be able to integrate OrayCSS into an existing site without unexpected destructive global overrides.

The baseline stylesheet may normalize reasonable defaults for:

- Box sizing
- Body margin
- Form element inheritance
- Media sizing
- Typography inheritance
- Focus visibility
- Consistent default behaviors

Do not globally remove meaningful accessibility indicators. Do not alter semantic elements unnecessarily.

Provide configuration options to enable, disable, or customize preflight. Specify the output order of reset rules, theme variables, utilities, variants, and user-authored CSS.

Existing CSS should continue to work. Do not globally force every element into a rigid component design.

