# 15. Custom CSS and Escape Hatches

OrayCSS must not trap developers inside utility classes.

Provide a simple, documented method for including ordinary authored CSS alongside generated utilities.

For example, a project should be able to maintain:

```css
/* site.css */

:root {
  --site-brand: #a78bfa;
}

.article-content {
  max-width: 72ch;
  margin-inline: auto;
}

.article-content h2 {
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
}
```

OrayCSS must not require users to rewrite all custom styles as utilities.

If custom utility directives or an `@apply` feature are introduced, implement them through a small, explicit, documented syntax. Do not claim complete CSS nesting, PostCSS, or Tailwind directive compatibility unless those capabilities are actually supported.

Keep utility compilation distinct from ordinary authored CSS processing.

